  "body": "## What changed\n\nBefore this change, `list_operation_types` listed only the fields that the default params serialize. Agents did not find optional fields (pocket `tilt` and `rest`, the plasma `feed` and pierce keys, the Wire Contour extras). Enum fields showed only `\"string\"`.\n\n- New module `crates/app/src/mcp/kind_fields.rs` with `kind_fields/trace.rs`. The trace runs the `Deserialize` of `ParamsDto` with a recording deserializer. It records the struct field names, the enum variant names and the `Option` fields of each kind. One rule applies to all kinds. The PR adds no hand list of field names.\n- Each field row now has these additions:\n  - `\"optional\": true` when the defaults do not write the field.\n  - `\"values\"` for an enum field (for example drill `cycle`, pocket `entry` and `strategy`, wire `side`).\n  - `\"shape\"` for an object or array field (for example `rest`, `tilt`, `tabs`, `links`). A `key?` in the shape is optional.\n- Two kinds flatten a struct (`#[serde(flatten)]`): `thread` and `sinker_side_burn`. Serde gives no key names for such a struct. Thus `kind_fields::flattened` traces the flattened type by itself, and it names the six optional keys of the thread variant.\n- A second small trace (`kind_fields/written.rs`, a recording serializer) gives the keys that the kind's params can write. A key that the type reads but never writes (`#[serde(skip_serializing)]`) is not offered. Example: the legacy wire `start`, which the load migrates into `picks`.\n- A kind that the trace cannot read gets `\"fields_incomplete\": true`. The pinning test fails on it.\n- The note of the tool tells what the new keys mean.\n- `job.rs` gets 5 more lines (it was already over 400). The new logic is in the new module.\n- Decision: `docs/decisions/3449-list-op-type-fields.md`.\n\n## Readings\n\n- Each kind is traced. Only the height fields (`retract_z`, `bottom_z`, face `top_z`) have the type `\"any\"`, because `HeightDto` reads itself (untagged).\n- The reply for one kind stays below the 4000-character budget. Measured replies: pocket 3604, sinker_side_burn 2123, wire_contour 2009, thread 1924, drill 1834, plasma_profile 1681, face 1563.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `op_type_fields::list_operation_types_reads_every_kind_completely` (binary `mcp`, new file `crates/app/tests/mcp/op_type_fields.rs` in the `tests/mcp/` directory suite). This is the Done clause: every kind is traced, no kind is incomplete, and no field is listed twice.\n- `op_type_fields::list_operation_types_names_the_optional_fields_and_enum_words`: pocket `tilt`/`rest`/`entry`, the Wire Contour extras and `tabs` shape, the plasma `feed`/`kerf`/`pierce_*`/`cut_height`, the drill `cycle` words, and the thread pass keys.\n- The existing pins also pass: `mcp_wire_contour::list_operation_types_and_skill_match_wire_contour_dto_and_tool_law` (the wire fields are the same as the DTO keys), `mcp_wire_contour::list_operation_types_says_the_wire_kind_mounts_a_wire_tool`, `mcp_compact::list_operation_types_filters_by_kind_and_by_section` (4000-character budget), `break_through::issue_2441_mcp_list_operation_types_lists_break_through`.\n- The pinning test also checks that the wire listing does not offer the legacy `start`.\n\n## Gate\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick` on the final head (Linux, `CAMCRAFT_GATE_JOBS=6`): 1215 steps, 1212 pass, 3 fail, 0 stall. All app, motion, kernel, post, sim and gpu steps pass. The 3 failed steps are UI steps that need a wgpu adapter. This host has no display and no `xvfb-run`:\n  - `ui suites: lib`: `egui_app::report_tests::*` and `egui_app::tests::headless_run_succeeds` panic with `Failed to create render state: CustomNativeAdapterSelectionError(\"No adapter found\")`.\n  - `ui suites: egui_app` (3 headless start tests) and `ui suites: shell` (`headless_cli_exit_code_is_zero`): the headless run returns 1 for the same reason.\n  - This PR changes no UI file. A runner with a display must run these 3 steps again.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- Serde cannot see a new optional key on the outer `thread` variant (a variant with a flatten), and the test does not find it. That one list of six names is written by hand.\n- Wire `condition` is required by the add_operation check, not by serde. The listing shows it as an optional field with the default `\"\"`, as before. It does not mark it as required.\n- The issue asks for a unit for each field. Serde has no unit, so this PR does not add units.\n- Light lane and heavy lanes: not run. No post or toolpath changed, and this is a P3 PR.\n- PR #4007 touches other files (UI and `tests/mcp_rotary_flow.rs`). No overlap.\n\nChangelog: MCP `list_operation_types` names every field that a kind accepts: optional fields are marked `optional`, enum fields list their `values`, and object fields show their `shape`.\n\nEffort: medium\n\nFixes #3449\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
